<title>FRANCE: ADP import traffic up 1.7pct in October.</title>
<headline>ADP import traffic up 1.7pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>October 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 45,113 tonnes, an increase of 1.7 percent on the same month last year, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>ADP imports by region in tonnes with percentage change from October 1995, were:</p>
<p>  Domestic		 2,658	down  1.1pct</p>
<p>  European Union	 6,095	up   14.6</p>
<p>  Non-EU Europe	  1,051	up    4.7</p>
<p>  North Africa	     676	down  5.6</p>
<p>  Sub-Saharan Africa   3,970	up    9.0</p>
<p>  North America	 15,373	down  4.8</p>
<p>  French territories     738	down  5.0</p>
<p>  Latin America	  1,533	down 15.2</p>
<p>  Middle East	    1,977	down  9.9</p>
<p>  Far East		11,042	up    8.2</p>
<p>  Total		   45,113	up    1.7</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
